#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# moment_of_inertia

#% text
# `moment_of_inertia(reg)` gives the inertia tensor of the region `reg` (unit density) about the origin; `moment_of_inertia(reg, p)` about the point `p`; `moment_of_inertia(reg, p, v)` the moment of inertia about the axis through `p` along `v`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The tensor is the integral of `|r|^2 I - r r^T` over the region, `r = x - p`; for a plane region it is `[[integrate(y^2), -integrate(x y)], [-integrate(x y), integrate(x^2)]]` (the plane components of the tensor of a thin plate).

#% item
# The moment about an axis is `v . I . v/(v . v)`.

#% item
# Implicit regions `x^2 + y^2 <= c` (with a range for `z`) are integrated as the disk (cylinder) they describe; cylinders along the z axis in cylindrical coordinates.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
moment_of_inertia(ball())
#% output
#= [[(8/15)*pi, 0, 0], [0, (8/15)*pi, 0], [0, 0, (8/15)*pi]]

#% cell
moment_of_inertia(ball(), [1, 1, 0])
#% output
#= [[(28/15)*pi, (-4/3)*pi, 0], [(-4/3)*pi, (28/15)*pi, 0], [0, 0, (16/5)*pi]]

#% cell
moment_of_inertia(ball(), [1, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1])
#% output
#= (16/5)*pi

#% cell
moment_of_inertia(rectangle([-l/2, -w/2], [l/2, w/2]))
#% output
#= [[(1/12)*l*w^3, 0], [0, (1/12)*w*l^3]]

#% cell
moment_of_inertia(cylinder([[0, 0, -h/2], [0, 0, h/2]], r))
#% output
#= [[(1/12)*h*pi*(3*r^2 + h^2)*r^2, 0, 0], [0, (1/12)*h*pi*(3*r^2 + h^2)*r^2, 0], [0, 0, (1/2)*h*pi*r^4]]

#% cell
moment_of_inertia(implicit_region(x^2 + y^2 <= 1, [x, y]))
#% output
#= [[(1/4)*pi, 0], [0, (1/4)*pi]]

